    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "39b0bf34352d6bb4aeb17920f959985091238db0",
      "message": "OTA-1862 \u2014 the beat keeps its way out (SE popup/modal small-viewport repair)\n\nThe owner reported, on a physical iPhone SE, that not every popup is\nresolution-aware and some run off the screen, and ruled it a confirmed UI\ndefect rather than a speculative audit. Constraint: SAME UI / SAME CONTENT /\nSAME INTERACTION / RESPONSIVE BOUNDS.\n\nONE PROVEN DEFECT CLASS. The kit carries two modal shells (OTA-1777).\n`modalCard` \u2014 the DIALOG \u2014 has capped its height at 85% since OTA-1614.\n`momentCard` \u2014 the BEAT \u2014 declared no ceiling at all. The asymmetry stayed\ninvisible because Family B's six adopters solve containment two ways:\nDogOnboarding, GolemNaming and WandererEncounter put the whole card INSIDE a\nScrollView that is a flex child of the scrim; CombatPrimer, MissionComplete and\nMissionStinger hang the card straight off `momentScrim`, whose centring pushes\noverflow off BOTH ends at once. Three of six were bounded by accident of\nconstruction and three were not bounded at all.\n\nMEASURED FROM THE AUTHORED CORPUS. A mission stinger is the worst real shape:\n`line` is `stageDef.stinger ?? stageDef.narration` and `granted` is the pack\nreceipt for a RANGE of stages. Across 50 arcs / 281 stages the ceilings are a\n403-character line (\"The Mud Titan of the Endless Stair\") and 8 grant-bearing\nstages in one arc (\"The Red Tower's Mouth\"). On the narrowest supported phone\nthat card wants 780pt in a 667pt window \u2014 113pt of overflow, centred, so ~56pt\nleft the screen at each end and the CTA went with the bottom. The arithmetic\nalso produced a finding: 0.85 x (932 - 48) = 751pt, so that beat overflows\nEVERY supported device; the SE only meets it soonest.\n\nTHE REPAIR IS GEOMETRY, AND ONLY GEOMETRY.\n- app/ui/tartariaKit.tsx: `momentCard` gains `maxHeight: '85%'` \u2014 the same\n  value, spelled the same way, that Family A already had. Inert for the three\n  that wrap: a percentage resolves against a parent with a DEFINITE size, and a\n  ScrollView's content container has none along its scroll axis.\n- MissionStingerModal: its card is PRIVATE by OTA-1777's governed exception\n  (\"remains EXPERIENTIAL\"), so the kit's ceiling does not reach it. Taking\n  `tMomentCard` would buy safety by reversing an owner ruling; the one value is\n  copied instead and the exception survives intact. Its prose, receipts and\n  next-line move into a ScrollView, title and rule pinned above, CTA pinned\n  below \u2014 OTA-1614's shape.\n- CombatPrimerModal / MissionCompleteModal: bodies gain `flexShrink: 1,\n  flexGrow: 0`, the pair BrandedModal's `scrollArea` has carried since\n  OTA-1799. Without it RN's `flexShrink: 0` default would push the pinned\n  control through the card's new bottom edge instead of yielding. Their own\n  360/380 reading windows are untouched \u2014 those are the card's, not the\n  screen's.\n\nNo content is deleted, shortened, hidden or conditionally omitted; a beat that\nalready fitted is laid out by exactly the tree it always was.\n\nCOVERAGE. New suite ota1862TheBeatKeepsItsWayOut, 23 tests: level-1 arithmetic\nover DEVICE_PROFILES reading the scrim gutter and the ceiling from the shipped\nstyles; a tree-wide RULE (a card that is a direct child of `momentScrim` must\ndeclare a ceiling) rather than three filenames, so the seventh moment modal\nfails here instead of on a phone; level-2 renders the real components and asks\nstructurally whether the data-sized region has a scrolling ancestor and the way\nout does not. Representative shapes A-E all covered.\n\nota1777's exhaustive shell assertion is amended, not weakened: the original\nseven values are still asserted exactly, with the new ceiling held separately.\n\nFour negative controls, applied and restored byte-exact, none committed:\nNC1 remove both ceilings -> 10 red; NC2 unscroll the stinger body -> reachability\nred; NC5 break the shared primitive while leaving the governed local exception\nintact -> 8 red, and the two exception tests correctly stay green; NC6 replace\nthe percentage with the fixed SE number -> 7 red including large-screen\npreservation. NC2 and NC5 each exposed a real gap in the suite (a vacuous\n0 === 0 equality, and an offender scan that trusted the primitive instead of\nreading it); both were widened before proceeding.\n\nValidation on this tree: 22/22 check gates, typecheck:ci, typecheck:tests\n(192 < 201 baseline), lint, and one test:ci:fast \u2014 1357/1357 suites,\n15548 passed / 3 skipped.\n\nSE regression covered in automation; physical-device confirmation pending\nowner observation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
